{"id":"13462600-0731-49cc-8087-0f64af321a60","object":"chat.completion","created":1784834281,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core_distance = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n    # Build mutual reachability edges with canonical order\\n    edges = []\\n    for a, b, d in distances:\\n        if a > b:\\n            a, b = b, a\\n        mut = max(core_distance[a], core_distance[b], d)\\n        edges.append((a, b, mut))\\n    # Sort by mutual reachability, then endpoints\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[2], x[0], x[1]))\\n    # Union-Find structure\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\\n        parent[ry] = rx\\n        if rank[rx] == rank[ry]:\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    for a, b, w in edges:\\n        if union(a, b):\\n            mst_edges.append([a, b, w])\\n            total_weight += w\\n            if len(mst_edges) == n - 1:\\n                break\\n    if len(mst_edges) != n - 1:\\n        return {'error': 'disconnected', 'edges': [], 'total_weight': 0.0}\\n    return {'edges': mst_edges, 'total_weight': total_weight}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a single JSON object with key \"implementation\" whose value is a JSON string containing the Python source code for `solve(case)`. The function must return a JSON-serializable object. The problem is about implementing HDBSCAN mutual reachability MST. Input case has nodes, core_distance