Functions find with path compression, union by rank.\n- Iterate sorted edges, if find(u) != find(v), union, add edge to mst_edges, accumulate total weight.\n- After loop, check len(mst_edges) == len(nodes)-1. If not, return error.\n- Return dict with \"edges\": list of [node1, node2, weight] (maintain canonical order) and \"total_weight\": float.\n\nCore distance is given as dict with node->float.\n\nReturn JSON-serializable object. So the solve function returns a dict.\n\nNow encode as JSON string inside the \"implementation\" value. Escape newlines, backslashes, quotes.\n\nWrite the Python source code as a multi-line string, then JSON escape it. I'll produce the JSON directly.\n\nBut the instruction says: \"Your entire response must be exactly one valid JSON object with the single key 'implementation'. The first non-whitespace character must be { and the last non-whitespace character must be }.\" So I need to output a JSON object like {\"implementation\": \"def solve(case): ...\"} with the source code as a string, properly escaped.\n\nI'll write the Python code and then manually escape. Better to generate the JSON using Python mentally. I'll produce the final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1541,"completion_tokens":1237,"total_tokens":2778,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1536},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":787},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1536,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":5},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}